  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Generally dry weather through next Sunday. \nDrought conditions will worsen.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nDry weather looks to persist through the end of next weekend.\nOver the past 24 hours, models have remained very unimpressive\nwith rain totals for the Thursday night/Friday cold front, and\nbacked off on any rain chances for Saturday night/Sunday. \n\nThis (Monday) afternoon, a cold front is moving from north to\nsouth through the area, and will move offshore this evening.\nThere is very little if any precipitation with the front.\nEarlier, a few spots got just enough rain to barely wet the\npavement, and that is about all we are looking for. Temperatures\nwill fall behind the front tonight, and we are looking at cool\ntemperatures through Wednesday before we warm up Thursday ahead\nof the next cold front.\n\nThe next cold front, expected to move through Thursday night\ninto Friday morning, will be much like its predecessors:\ngenerally dry, with any localized rain amounts being less than\n0.10 inch.\n\nQuiet, dry weather with temperatures fairly close to average are\nin store for the weekend. As said before, any rain chances\nshould hold off until Sunday night at the earliest. Models are\nin pretty good agreement on dry weather through Sunday, but\ndisagree significantly after Sunday on when/if any rain comes.",
